Z||000000||Loki||03-08-2001||12:49 AM||||Its attached to the corner of the head. On my car its on the side facing the trunk on the end of the TB. On other it may be on back side close to battery. Im needing to replace it and not sure what it is. Also where is the snsor that controls the temp gauge?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki137/loki5.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||03-08-2001||01:47 AM||||I think that you are describing the sensor that controls the temp gauge!! -- located on the left of the block close to the manifold and inline with the distributor, right? - two wires, a green wire and a green/yellow wire? -- that is one of the coolant temp sensors......of the two wires, one controls the gauge and one controls the light........<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">      </A><P>87 GT<BR>87 GT<BR>87 GT<BR>88 Coupe<BR>88 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||03-08-2001||03:08 PM||||tgowens is right (as usual).  On the other (forward) head, that threaded hole near the battery is normally plugged.<P>When it comes to holes in the head, I usually know what I'm talking about  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
